Why This Matters
Managing multiple hosts in RHVM is crucial for:

High Availability: Multiple hosts provide redundancy and failover capabilities
Load Distribution: Workloads can be spread across multiple physical servers
Maintenance Windows: Hosts can be maintained without service interruption
Scalability: Infrastructure can grow to meet increasing demands
Resource Optimization: Better utilization of hardware resources across the environment
This knowledge prepares you for real-world virtualization environments where managing multiple hosts efficiently is essential for maintaining reliable and scalable infrastructure services. These skills are directly applicable to the Red Hat Certified Specialist in Virtualization exam and professional virtualization management roles.
